						"Notes": "This model calculates component molar flows and energy duty for simultaneous reactions based on fractional conversions.\n\nFeed component flows (FeedFlows) are determined from the inlet stream. Reaction extents (calcExtents) are solved simultaneously from the linear system A * xi = b using the reaction stoichiometry, key component indices, and target conversions (Extents).\n\nProduct component flows (ReactCmpF) are calculated as FeedFlows + Stoichiometry * calcExtents and verified for non-negative values with minusCheck. The product stream (ReactOut) is flashed at OutletT and OutletP, and the net reactor heat duty (ReactorQ) is calculated from the enthalpy difference between outlet and feed streams plus the standard heats of reaction (HeatRxn).",
